# NES: the dump starts about 1 s after the game's first write (the debounce used
# to be 2 s), through the real iosys, SDRAM and save engine. A player who saves
# and presses MODE a second or two later keeps the save. (Sim time stretches the
# dump itself, so the test times its start and then waits for the file.)
expect-screen "TangCore"
press b
expect-screen "game.nes"
press down
press a
expect-overlay off
expect-core nestang
wram-burst 0x000 512 0xA5
wait-dump 1300ms
expect-file saves/nes/game.sav size 8192
